(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the projections of a straight line in various standard positions relative to reference planes: parallel to both, perpendicular to one, and parallel to one while inclined to the other.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Line Parallel to Both HP and VP:) Tj
T*
(   - Both front view \(a'b'\) and top view \(ab\) are parallel to reference line XY.) Tj
T*
(   - Both views show the TRUE LENGTH \(TL\) of the line: a'b' = ab = TL.) Tj
T*
(   - The line possesses no Horizontal Trace \(HT\) and no Vertical Trace \(VT\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
