(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define the concept of Traces of a straight line \(Horizontal Trace and Vertical Trace\), explaining the step-by-step geometric procedure to locate them from the front and top views.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Definition of Traces:) Tj
T*
(   - Traces are the piercing points where a straight line \(or its collinear extension in space\)) Tj
T*
(   intersects the principal planes of projection.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal Trace \(HT\): The physical point of intersection of the line with the Horizontal) Tj
T*
(   Plane \(HP\).) Tj
T*
(   * Since HT lies on HP, its vertical elevation must lie on the ground line XY. Thus, the front) Tj
T*
(   view of HT \(denoted h'\) always lies on the XY line. The top view of HT \(denoted h\) is the) Tj
T*
(   actual trace.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Trace \(VT\): The physical point of intersection of the line with the Vertical Plane) Tj
T*
(   \(VP\).) Tj
T*
(   * Since VT lies on VP, its distance from VP is zero. Thus, the top view of VT \(denoted v\)) Tj
T*
(   always lies on the XY line. The front view of VT \(denoted v'\) is the actual trace.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Procedure to Locate Horizontal Trace \(HT\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Extend the front view a'b' \(if necessary\) until it intersects the reference line XY) Tj
T*
(   at point h'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: From point h', draw a vertical projector line perpendicular to the XY line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Extend the top view ab \(in the same direction\) until it intersects this vertical) Tj
T*
(   projector.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: The intersection point is the top view 'h', which is the required Horizontal Trace) Tj
T*
(   \(HT\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Procedure to Locate Vertical Trace \(VT\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Extend the top view ab until it intersects the reference line XY at point v.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: From point v, draw a vertical projector line perpendicular to the XY line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Extend the front view a'b' until it intersects this vertical projector.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: The intersection point is the front view 'v'', which is the required Vertical Trace) Tj
T*
(   \(VT\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

