/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Trapezoid Method for determining the true length and true inclinations of an inclined straight line, comparing it with the rotating line method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundation of the Trapezoid Method:) Tj
T*
(   - When a straight line AB in space is projected onto HP, the projectors Aa and Bb are) Tj
T*
(   perpendicular to HP and therefore parallel to each other.) Tj
T*
(   - In 3D space, the quadrilateral formed by A-B-b-a is a right-angled trapezoid where:) Tj
T*
(   * Side ab is the Plan Length \(PL\).) Tj
T*
(   * Parallel sides Aa and Bb represent the heights of points A and B above HP \(zA and zB\).) Tj
T*
(   * The hypotenuse AB is the TRUE LENGTH \(TL\) of the line!) Tj
T*
(   * The angle between AB and ab is the true inclination with HP \(theta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Drafting Procedure for Trapezoid on Top View:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw the top view ab of the given line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: At point 'a', erect a perpendicular to line ab of length equal to height of a' above) Tj
T*
(   XY \(zA\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: At point 'b', erect a perpendicular to line ab on the same side of length equal to) Tj
T*
(   height of b' above XY \(zB\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Join the endpoints of these perpendiculars. The length of this connecting line is the) Tj
T*
(   TRUE LENGTH \(TL\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: The angle between this line and ab is the true angle theta.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Trapezoid on Front View \(to find phi\):) Tj
T*
(   - At front view points a' and b', erect perpendiculars to a'b' equal to distances of a and b) Tj
T*
(   from XY \(yA and yB\).) Tj
T*
(   - Joining the ends gives the True Length \(TL\) and true angle phi with VP!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
