(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Auxiliary Plane Method for finding the true length and inclinations of a straight line inclined to both reference planes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Auxiliary Planes:) Tj
T*
(   - An Auxiliary Plane is an imaginary reference plane set up perpendicular to one principal) Tj
T*
(   plane and inclined to the other.) Tj
T*
(   - Auxiliary Vertical Plane \(AVP\): Perpendicular to HP and inclined to VP.) Tj
T*
(   - Auxiliary Inclined Plane \(AIP\): Perpendicular to VP and inclined to HP.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Procedure to Find True Length and theta using AVP:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Obtain the top view 'ab' of the line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Set up an Auxiliary Vertical Plane parallel to the line AB by drawing a new reference) Tj
T*
(   line X1Y1 PARALLEL to top view 'ab'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: From points 'a' and 'b', draw auxiliary projectors perpendicular to X1Y1.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Along these projectors, transfer the distances of front views a' and b' from the) Tj
T*
(   original XY line \(heights zA and zB\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Connect the newly plotted points a1' and b1'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Line a1'b1' represents the TRUE LENGTH \(TL\) of line AB!) Tj
T*
(   - Step 7: The angle between a1'b1' and X1Y1 is the true angle of inclination with HP \(theta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Procedure to Find True Angle phi using AIP:) Tj
T*
(   - Draw new reference line X2Y2 parallel to front view a'b'.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw projectors perpendicular to X2Y2 and transfer distances of plan points a and b from) Tj
T*
(   original XY.) Tj
T*
(   - The resulting view gives True Length and true inclination with VP \(phi\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
