(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the AutoCAD commands used for precision line drafting: LINE, dynamic input options, relative polar input syntax, and ortho/polar tracking toggles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. LINE Command Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE \(or 'L' [Enter]\)) Tj
T*
(   - Prompts for start point: Can be specified via mouse click, absolute coordinates \(X,Y\), or) Tj
T*
(   OSNAP pick.) Tj
T*
(   - Successive Prompts: 'Specify next point or [Undo]:' continues line chaining.) Tj
T*
(   - Pressing 'C' closes the loop back to the start point; pressing 'U' undoes the last segment) Tj
T*
(   without canceling the command.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Relative Polar Coordinate Syntax \(@Distance < Angle\):) Tj
T*
(   - Critical for drawing lines of known length at specific angles.) Tj
T*
(   - Format: @length<angle \(e.g. '@80<30'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Direction: In AutoCAD, angle 0? is along positive X-axis \(East\), and angles increase) Tj
T*
(   counterclockwise.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative angles \(e.g. '@80<-45'\) measure clockwise.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
