(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the POLYLINE \(PLINE\) command in AutoCAD, contrasting it with the LINE command and detailing sub-options: Arc, Halfwidth, Length, Undo, and Width.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Polyline vs Standard Line:) Tj
T*
(   - A Polyline is a 2D composite object consisting of connected linear segments and circular arc) Tj
T*
(   segments treated by AutoCAD as a SINGLE unified database entity.) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages over LINE:) Tj
T*
(   * Unified selection: Clicking any segment selects the entire boundary.) Tj
T*
(   * Assignable line thickness \(width\) that plots with solid fills.) Tj
T*
(   * Direct area, perimeter, and centroid calculation via AREA and MASSPROP commands.) Tj
T*
(   * Can be converted to 3D solid profiles via EXTRUDE without boundary sealing issues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Key PLINE Sub-Options:) Tj
T*
(   - Width \(W\): Prompts for 'Starting width' and 'Ending width'. Setting start = 0 and end = 5 mm) Tj
T*
(   creates an arrow; setting start = end = 2 mm creates a thick trace.) Tj
T*
(   - Halfwidth \(H\): Specifies width measured from the center line to the outer edge \(half of total) Tj
T*
(   width\).) Tj
T*
(   - Arc \(A\): Switches the polyline from drawing straight lines to drawing tangent circular arcs) Tj
T*
(   seamlessly.) Tj
T*
(   * Inside Arc mode, sub-options like Angle, Center, Direction, Radius, and Line \(L - to switch) Tj
T*
(   back to straight lines\) become active.) Tj
T*
(   - Length \(L\): Prompts for a distance and continues the next line segment in the exact same) Tj
T*
(   direction as the prior segment.) Tj
T*
(   - Close \(C\): Connects current vertex back to the start point and terminates command.) Tj
T*
(   - Undo \(U\): Erases the last vertex segment while keeping command active.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
