(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the POLYGON command in AutoCAD, contrasting Inscribed and Circumscribed methods and detailing the Edge construction method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. POLYGON Command Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: POLYGON \(or 'POL' [Enter]\)) Tj
T*
(   - First Prompt: 'Enter number of sides <4>:' \(Accepts integers from 3 up to 1024\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Center-Based Construction Methods:) Tj
T*
(   - Pick a center point. AutoCAD prompts: 'Enter an option [Inscribed in circle/Circumscribed) Tj
T*
(   about circle] <I>:'.) Tj
T*
(   - Inscribed in Circle \(I\):) Tj
T*
(   * All polygon vertices lie precisely on the circumference of an imaginary circle of specified) Tj
T*
(   radius R.) Tj
T*
(   * The radius corresponds to the distance from center to VERTEX.) Tj
T*
(   * Formula for edge length 's' of an n-sided polygon: s = 2 * R * sin\(180? / n\).) Tj
T*
(   - Circumscribed About Circle \(C\):) Tj
T*
(   * The midpoints of all polygon edges lie tangent to the imaginary circle of radius R.) Tj
T*
(   * The radius corresponds to the distance from center to the MIDPOINT of an edge \(apothem\).) Tj
T*
(   * Formula for edge length 's': s = 2 * R * tan\(180? / n\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Edge Method \(E\):) Tj
T*
(   - Rather than specifying center and radius, the user types 'E' [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Prompts: 'Specify first endpoint of edge:' -> 'Specify second endpoint of edge:'.) Tj
T*
(   - AutoCAD constructs a perfect regular polygon with side length equal to the distance between) Tj
T*
(   the two picked points, aligned to their angle.) Tj
T*
(   - This is the fastest and most accurate method when drawing regular polygons aligned to) Tj
T*
(   existing machine features.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
