(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the dimensioning commands for lines and angles in AutoCAD: DIMLINEAR, DIMALIGNED, DIMANGULAR, and DIMCONTINUE.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. DIMLINEAR \(DLI\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates linear horizontal or vertical dimensions.) Tj
T*
(   - Prompts: Specify first extension line origin -> Specify second origin -> Specify dimension) Tj
T*
(   line location.) Tj
T*
(   - Behavior: Even if two points are picked along an inclined line, DIMLINEAR forces the) Tj
T*
(   dimension to measure strictly the projected horizontal \(dx\) or vertical \(dy\) distance depending) Tj
T*
(   on cursor placement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. DIMALIGNED \(DAL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates a linear dimension aligned strictly parallel to the two picked points.) Tj
T*
(   - Behavior: Measures the true 3D inclined straight-line distance between features.) Tj
T*
(   - Essential for dimensioning true lengths of sloping edges and inclined shafts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. DIMANGULAR \(DAN\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Measures the angle between two non-parallel line entities, or the included angle of) Tj
T*
(   an arc, or angle between three points.) Tj
T*
(   - Prompts: Select first line -> Select second line -> Specify dimension arc line location.) Tj
T*
(   - Displays dimension text with degree symbol \(?\) automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. DIMCONTINUE \(DCO\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Automatically continues a series of chain dimensions starting from the second) Tj
T*
(   extension line of the previously placed dimension.) Tj
T*
