(   [Problem Statement]: A line MN has its front view m'n' measuring 50 mm inclined at 30 degrees to XY, and top view mn measuring 60 mm inclined at 45 degrees to XY. End M is in HP and 20 mm in front of VP. Determine its true length and true angles theta and phi.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Projections Data:) Tj
T*
(   - End M: In HP => z_m = 0 \(m' is on XY line\); y_m = 20 mm in front of VP \(m is 20 mm below XY\).) Tj
T*
(   - Elevation Length EL = 50 mm, apparent angle alpha = 30 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Plan Length PL = 60 mm, apparent angle beta = 45 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Coordinate Determination of Other End N:) Tj
T*
(   - For Front View m'n':) Tj
T*
(   m' is at \(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   n' is at: x_n = EL * cos\(alpha\) = 50 * cos\(30?\) = 50 * 0.8660 = 43.30 mm.) Tj
T*
ET

