(   Height of n' above XY: z_n = EL * sin\(alpha\) = 50 * sin\(30?\) = 25.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - For Top View mn:) Tj
T*
(   m is at \(0, -20\).) Tj
T*
(   Since both views of N must share the same projector, the x-coordinate of n must equal x_n =) Tj
T*
(   43.30 mm!) Tj
T*
(   Top view length PL = sqrt\( \(x_n - x_m\)^2 + \(y_n - y_m\)^2 \) = 60 mm.) Tj
T*
(   \(43.30\)^2 + \(Delta Y\)^2 = 60^2) Tj
T*
(   1875 + \(Delta Y\)^2 = 3600 => \(Delta Y\)^2 = 1725 => Delta Y = sqrt\(1725\) = 41.53 mm.) Tj
T*
(   y_n = y_m + Delta Y = 20 + 41.53 = 61.53 mm in front of VP \(or 20 - 41.53 = -21.53 behind VP\).) Tj
T*
(   Assuming both ends in 1st quadrant: y_n = 61.53 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. True Length \(TL\) Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - TL = sqrt\( \(Delta X\)^2 + \(Delta Y\)^2 + \(Delta Z\)^2 \)) Tj
T*
(   - TL = sqrt\( 43.30^2 + 41.53^2 + 25.00^2 \)) Tj
T*
(   - TL = sqrt\( 1875 + 1725 + 625 \) = sqrt\( 4225 \) = 65.00 mm! \(Exact integer root\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. True Inclination Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Inclination with HP \(theta\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta\) = Delta Z / TL = 25.00 / 65.00 = 0.3846 => theta = 22.62 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Inclination with VP \(phi\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(phi\) = Delta Y / TL = 41.53 / 65.00 = 0.6389 => phi = 39.71 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Final Verification:) Tj
T*
(   EL = TL * cos\(phi\) = 65 * cos\(39.71?\) = 65 * 0.7692 = 50.00 mm. \(Matches given EL!\)) Tj
T*
(   PL = TL * cos\(theta\) = 65 * cos\(22.62?\) = 65 * 0.9231 = 60.00 mm. \(Matches given PL!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
