/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Grade or Slope of a line in civil and mechanical engineering drawings, relating percentage slope to the true inclination angle theta.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Engineering Definition of Grade \(Slope\):) Tj
T*
(   - In civil engineering \(roads, railway tracks, drainage pipelines\) and structural engineering) Tj
T*
(   \(roof trusses, ramps\), the inclination of a line relative to the horizontal datum is commonly) Tj
T*
(   specified as a 'Grade' or 'Slope' rather than an angular degree measurement.) Tj
T*
(   - Grade is defined mathematically as the ratio of vertical rise \(Delta Z\) to horizontal run) Tj
T*
(   \(horizontal plan distance PL\):) Tj
T*
(   Slope \(m\) = Rise / Run = Delta Z / PL = tan\(theta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Representations of Grade:) Tj
T*
(   - Fractional Slope \(1 in N\): A rise of 1 vertical unit over N horizontal units \(e.g. 1 in 20\).) Tj
T*
(   tan\(theta\) = 1 / N => theta = atan\(1 / N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Percentage Grade: The vertical rise per 100 units of horizontal run:) Tj
T*
(   Grade \(%\) = \(Rise / Run\) * 100 = tan\(theta\) * 100.) Tj
T*
(   Example: A 5% road grade means tan\(theta\) = 0.05 => theta = 2.86 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Bearing of a Line:) Tj
T*
(   - In surveying and civil drawings, the plan direction is specified by its compass Bearing:) Tj
T*
(   - Whole Circle Bearing \(WCB\): 0? to 360? measured clockwise from True North.) Tj
T*
(   - Quadrantal Bearing \(QB\): Measured from North or South towards East or West \(e.g., N 45? E\).) Tj
T*
(   - The bearing corresponds directly to the angle made by the top view \(plan\) of the line) Tj
T*
(   relative to the meridian.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

