(   [Problem Statement]: A line AB 90 mm long has end A 25 mm above HP and 20 mm in front of VP. End B is 70 mm above HP and 60 mm in front of VP. Find the true inclinations theta and phi, apparent angles alpha and beta, and draw the projections.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometric Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   - A: zA = 25 mm, yA = 20 mm) Tj
T*
(   - B: zB = 70 mm, yB = 60 mm) Tj
T*
(   - True Length TL = 90 mm) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Rise: Delta Z = 70 - 25 = 45 mm) Tj
T*
(   - Depth Difference: Delta Y = 60 - 20 = 40 mm) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. True Angles Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - Inclination with HP \(theta\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta\) = Delta Z / TL = 45 / 90 = 0.5000 => theta = 30.00 degrees!) Tj
T*
(   - Inclination with VP \(phi\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(phi\) = Delta Y / TL = 40 / 90 = 0.4444 => phi = 26.39 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Apparent Lengths Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - Plan Length \(PL\):) Tj
T*
(   PL = TL * cos\(theta\) = 90 * cos\(30?\) = 90 * 0.8660 = 77.94 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Elevation Length \(EL\):) Tj
T*
(   EL = TL * cos\(phi\) = 90 * cos\(26.39?\) = 90 * 0.8958 = 80.62 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Distance between Projectors \(D\):) Tj
T*
(   D = sqrt\( PL^2 - \(Delta Y\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 77.94^2 - 40^2 \) = sqrt\( 6075 - 1600 \) = sqrt\( 4475 \) =) Tj
T*
(   66.90 mm.) Tj
T*
(   Verify via EL: D = sqrt\( EL^2 - \(Delta Z\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 80.62^2 - 45^2 \) = sqrt\( 6500 - 2025 \) =) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\( 4475 \) = 66.90 mm. \(Perfect consistency!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Apparent Angles:) Tj
T*
(   - Elevation Angle alpha:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(alpha\) = Delta Z / D = 45 / 66.90 = 0.6726 => alpha = 33.93 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Plan Angle beta:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(beta\) = Delta Y / D = 40 / 66.90 = 0.5979 => beta = 30.88 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
