(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how to determine the shortest perpendicular distance from a given point to an inclined straight line using orthographic projections and auxiliary views.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - The true perpendicular distance from a point P to a straight line AB can be viewed in its) Tj
T*
(   true dimension ONLY when the straight line AB is viewed as a SINGLE POINT \(point view / end-on) Tj
T*
(   view\).) Tj
T*
(   - In a point view of line AB, any perpendicular line drawn from point P to AB is parallel to) Tj
T*
(   the projection plane and hence displays its true geometric length.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Auxiliary Plane Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw the primary front view \(a'b'\) and top view \(ab\) of the line, along with the) Tj
T*
(   views of point P \(p' and p\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(First Auxiliary View - True Length of Line\):) Tj
T*
(   * Set up a reference line X1Y1 parallel to one of the views \(e.g. parallel to top view ab\).) Tj
T*
(   * Project points a, b, and p perpendicular to X1Y1.) Tj
T*
(   * Transfer heights from original front view.) Tj
T*
(   * In this auxiliary view, line a1b1 shows its TRUE LENGTH \(TL\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Second Auxiliary View - Point View of Line\):) Tj
T*
