(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the geometric method to find the true angle between two intersecting straight lines in space using auxiliary planes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis:) Tj
T*
(   - Two intersecting straight lines AB and AC define a unique planar surface in 3D space.) Tj
T*
(   - The true angle between them \(angle BAC\) can only be measured directly in a projection view) Tj
T*
(   where the plane containing both lines is parallel to the projection plane \(i.e. True Shape view) Tj
T*
(   of plane ABC\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Method:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Construct the front views \(a'b', a'c'\) and top views \(ab, ac\) of the intersecting) Tj
T*
(   lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Draw a horizontal line in the front view from b' intersecting a'c' at point d'.) Tj
T*
(   Project d' down to top view ac to obtain d. Line bd is a true horizontal line on the plane,) Tj
T*
(   meaning its top view bd shows TRUE LENGTH.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(First Auxiliary View - Edge View of Plane\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw reference line X1Y1 perpendicular to the true length line bd.) Tj
T*
(   * Project points a, b, c onto X1Y1 and transfer front view heights.) Tj
T*
(   * Because line bd is viewed end-on as a point, the entire plane ABC appears as a single) Tj
T*
(   straight edge line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Second Auxiliary View - True Shape View\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw reference line X2Y2 parallel to the edge view line of plane ABC.) Tj
T*
(   * Project points a, b, c perpendicular to X2Y2.) Tj
T*
(   * In this view, both lines AB and AC display their true lengths simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Measure the angle between a2b2 and a2c2 with a protractor. This is the TRUE ANGLE) Tj
T*
(   between the two intersecting spatial lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
