(   [Problem Statement]: A straight line AB has its end A in the HP and 25 mm in front of VP. End B is in the VP and 40 mm above HP. The distance between the end projectors is 45 mm. Draw the projections, find the true length, true angles, and mark the traces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Position Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - End A: In HP => zA = 0 \(a' is on XY line\); yA = 25 mm \(a is 25 mm below XY\).) Tj
T*
(   - End B: In VP => yB = 0 \(b is on XY line\); zB = 40 mm \(b' is 40 mm above XY\).) Tj
T*
(   - Distance between projectors D = 45 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Identification of Traces:) Tj
T*
(   - Because end A lies directly in the HP, its top view 'a' is the HORIZONTAL TRACE \(HT\)!) Tj
T*
(   HT is located 25 mm in front of VP on projector A.) Tj
T*
(   - Because end B lies directly in the Vertical Plane, its front view 'b'' is the VERTICAL TRACE) Tj
T*
(   \(VT\)!) Tj
T*
(   VT is located 40 mm above HP on projector B.) Tj
T*
