12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Skew Lines in descriptive geometry, defining their shortest distance and detailing how to determine if two spatial lines intersect.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Skew Lines:) Tj
T*
(   - Skew lines are straight lines in three-dimensional space that are neither parallel to each) Tj
T*
(   other nor intersecting.) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike coplanar lines, skew lines do not lie within any common geometric plane.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Test for Intersection of Two Lines AB and CD:) Tj
T*
(   - Two lines in space intersect if and only if their apparent point of intersection in the front) Tj
T*
(   view and their apparent point of intersection in the top view lie on the exact same vertical) Tj
T*
(   projector!) Tj
T*
(   - Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   * Locate apparent crossing point 1' of a'b' and c'd' in front view.) Tj
T*
(   * Project 1' vertically down to the top view.) Tj
T*
(   * If projector 1' intersects lines ab and cd at their apparent crossing point 1, the lines) Tj
T*
(   physically intersect in 3D space.) Tj
T*
(   * If the projector intersects ab and cd at two separate points, the lines are SKEW lines that) Tj
T*
(   cross in visual projection but have a clearance distance in 3D space.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Shortest Distance Between Two Skew Lines:) Tj
T*
(   - The shortest distance between two skew lines is the length of a unique line segment that is) Tj
T*
(   simultaneously perpendicular to both skew lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Determined via auxiliary projections by obtaining a view where one line appears as a point;) Tj
T*
(   the perpendicular dropped from this point to the second line is the true shortest distance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
