12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A line AB 85 mm long has its end A 25 mm above HP and 20 mm in front of VP. The line is inclined at 40 degrees to HP. The distance between the end projectors is 60 mm. Find the inclination of the line with VP and draw its projections.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Information:) Tj
T*
(   - True Length TL = 85 mm) Tj
T*
(   - End A: zA = 25 mm, yA = 20 mm) Tj
T*
(   - Angle with HP: theta = 40 degrees) Tj
T*
(   - Distance between projectors: D = 60 mm) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical rise: Delta Z = TL * sin\(theta\) = 85 * sin\(40?\) = 85 * 0.6428 = 54.64 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Height of end B: zB = zA + Delta Z = 25 + 54.64 = 79.64 mm above HP.) Tj
T*
(   - Plan Length \(PL\): PL = TL * cos\(theta\) = 85 * cos\(40?\) = 85 * 0.7660 = 65.11 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Distance between projectors D = 60 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - We know that for plan view ab:) Tj
T*
(   PL = sqrt\( D^2 + \(Delta Y\)^2 \)) Tj
T*
(   65.11^2 = 60^2 + \(Delta Y\)^2) Tj
T*
(   4239.31 = 3600 + \(Delta Y\)^2) Tj
T*
(   \(Delta Y\)^2 = 4239.31 - 3600 = 639.31) Tj
T*
(   Delta Y = sqrt\(639.31\) = 25.28 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Distance of end B in front of VP: yB = yA + Delta Y = 20 + 25.28 = 45.28 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. True Inclination with VP \(phi\):) Tj
T*
(   - sin\(phi\) = Delta Y / TL = 25.28 / 85 = 0.2974) Tj
T*
(   - phi = asin\(0.2974\) = 17.30 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
