12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Profile Plane \(PP\) projection for profile lines \(lines perpendicular to XY reference line\), detailing how end-views are constructed using a 45-degree miter line.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nature of Profile Lines:) Tj
T*
(   - A profile line is a straight line inclined to both HP and VP such that the sum of its true) Tj
T*
(   angles equals 90 degrees \(theta + phi = 90?\).) Tj
T*
(   - In standard orthographic projection, both the front view \(a'b'\) and the top view \(ab\) are) Tj
T*
(   PERPENDICULAR to the reference line XY, lying along the exact same vertical projector line.) Tj
T*
(   - Because the views overlap collinearly, true length and true angles cannot be determined from) Tj
T*
(   front and top views alone; an Auxiliary Profile View \(Side View / End View\) is mandatory!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Construction of Profile Plane \(X1Y1\) and 45-Degree Miter Line:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw a vertical profile reference line X1Y1 perpendicular to XY at a convenient) Tj
T*
(   distance to the right of the line projector.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: From the intersection origin O \(where XY and X1Y1 meet\), draw a miter line inclined) Tj
T*
(   at 45 degrees into the fourth quadrant \(below XY and to the right of X1Y1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: From top views a and b, project horizontal lines to the right until they intersect) Tj
T*
(   the 45-degree miter line.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: From these intersection points on the miter line, project vertical lines upward into) Tj
T*
(   the first quadrant \(above XY\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: From front views a' and b', project horizontal lines to the right to intersect the) Tj
T*
(   corresponding vertical projectors from step 4.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Label the intersections a" and b". The line segment a"b" is the SIDE VIEW \(PROFILE) Tj
T*
(   VIEW\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 7: Since the line is parallel to the profile plane, its side view a"b" displays its TRUE) Tj
T*
(   LENGTH \(TL\) and true inclinations!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
