12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of drawing smooth non-circular curves in AutoCAD: SPLINE \(Fit Points vs Control Vertices\) and PEDIT Spline/Fit conversion of polylines.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. SPLINE Command \(NURBS Curves\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SPLINE \(or 'SPL' [Enter]\)) Tj
T*
(   - Constructs a Non-Uniform Rational B-Spline curve passing smoothly through or influenced by a) Tj
T*
(   set of points.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Spline Creation Methods:) Tj
T*
(   - Fit Points Method \(Default\):) Tj
T*
(   * The spline curve physically passes directly through every clicked point.) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts for start point, subsequent through points, and start/end tangency directions.) Tj
T*
(   * Ideal for plotting points from experimental data or calculated trace trajectories.) Tj
T*
(   - Control Vertices \(CV\) Method:) Tj
T*
(   * Points picked define an external bounding 'control polygon'.) Tj
T*
(   * The spline is pulled toward the control vertices by polynomial weighting without passing) Tj
T*
(   through them \(except start and end points\).) Tj
T*
